Fix vLLM 0.15.1 crashing on multimodal (Qwen3-VL) checkpoints under
transformers >= 5.x.

vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3.py reads `tie_word_embeddings` from the TEXT
config. For a multimodal model the text config is a Qwen3VLTextConfig, and
transformers 5.x keeps that flag on the COMPOSITE config only, so the lookup
raises

    AttributeError: 'Qwen3VLTextConfig' object has no attribute 'tie_word_embeddings'

and the engine core dies while loading the checkpoint:

    AttributeError: 'Qwen3VLTextConfig' object has no attribute 'tie_word_embeddings'
    ...
    RuntimeError: Engine core initialization failed.

Use getattr() so the declared value is still honoured when the attribute does
exist (e.g. plain Qwen3 text models) and the safe default is used otherwise.
For RoboBrain2.5-8B-NV the correct value is False: config.json declares
`tie_word_embeddings: false` at the top level and the checkpoint stores
`lm_head.weight`, so the LM head must be loaded, not skipped.

--- a/vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3.py
@@ -394,7 +394,7 @@
     def load_weights(self, weights: Iterable[tuple[str, torch.Tensor]]) -> set[str]:
         loader = AutoWeightsLoader(
             self,
-            skip_prefixes=(["lm_head."] if self.config.tie_word_embeddings else None),
+            skip_prefixes=(["lm_head."] if getattr(self.config, "tie_word_embeddings", False) else None),
         )
         return loader.load_weights(weights)
